 i honestly have no idea what this film  is about  and i'm eight weeks into shooting it he  says that he's only slightly kidding  now he says that this is mostly due to  sony and marvel believing that he is  going to spoil what is actually going to  happen  which i wholeheartedly believe however  last week  he also said that it was the most  ambitious standalone superhero film  ever to be made that's a pretty bold  statement to make  if you don't know what the movie is  really about he specifically said  i have no idea what this film is about  so at this point it really does seem  like tom holland and sony and marvel are  really just trying to throw us off  on what the movie could be about if he  didn't know what the movie was about he  clearly couldn't know that it's the most  ambitious  standalone film ever as far as the  superhero world was concerned so for  those of you who were worried that he  said standalone film  i think that's just tom holland trying  to throw people off the multiverse trail  and just him trying to get people hyped  for the movie because the same week he  said that the movie was absolutely  insane but he also said that for  spider-man far from home  tom has been known to spoil a few things  here and there so i'm guessing they  haven't really told him much yet  however they did go on to ask him about  the spider-verse and talked about all of  the rumors and reports about casting  decisions and the other  spider-man from other universes showing  up and even the person doing the  interview seemed to catch on that tom  holland had different answers for  certain things  tom holland went from knowing nothing  about the film  to having an absolute answer about the  spider-verse the interviewer said when i  asked  holland about this possibility referring  to the spider-verse  he is suddenly positive he knows what  he's talking about so again even the  interviewer said  he went from knowing nothing to all of a  sudden he's positive he knows everything  but tom holland did go on to say no no  they will not be appearing in the film  unless they have hidden the most massive  piece of information from me which i  think is too big of a secret for them to  keep from me  but as of yet no it'll be a continuation  of the spider-man movies that we've been  making  now this could actually be true or he  may not know about them yet  however we've had multiple reports from  very very credible media outlets stating  that alfred molina's doc octa is coming  back  and jamie foxx's electro was coming back  which doesn't really make sense unless  the multiverse is involved in some way  shape or form which we know it will be  because kevin feige said one division  leads into spider-man 3 and it looks  like  the multiverse is being torn apart in  one division since the last episode  so although this could be true i think  tom is under specific instructions that  if anybody asks him  anything about spider-man 3 he is to  deny the fact that it is a multiverse  film  now of course everybody could be wrong  and it could indeed just be a regular  spider-man film  but again there have been so many  reports from credible people stating  that it is a spider-verse film i'd be  surprised if it wasn't  in fact even today we have a report from  daniel richmond stating that  although toby maguire was having some  issues with the contract for spider-man  3 before he has now  officially signed up for the film and  he's going to have multiple costumes  according to daniel rbk  again it just seems like there have been  too many reports from very credible  sources to say that the multiverse isn't  going to happen  and besides what is tom holland actually  going to say when asked about this he's  not going to be like oh yeah toby and  andrew are great i can't wait for  everybody to see all three spider-man on  screen together in this huge multiverse  film  there's just no way that can happen he  can't really say anything about it  because sony and marvel want him to keep  his mouth shut so i'm not really buying  this  especially because last week he was  talking about the movie and how great  and huge it's going to be and then this  week he said that he doesn't know  anything about it  it just seems like he's trying to hype  the movie up without giving anything  away about it but let me know what you  think about this do you think that tom  holland is telling the truth and do you  think that if he  isn't and it is a multiverse film he'll  spoil it soon it seems like marvel's  being super strict about this one but  we'll see about that so let me know your  thoughts in the comments down below  don't forget to subscribe so you can  stay up to date on all news relating to  spider-man 3.  don't forget to like the video and for  live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter  as always thank you all so much for  watching woof  hmm

